# Local AI-agent tool state — never part of the project's own history
.claude/
**/.claude/

# Android / Gradle build output (once app development starts — see ARCHITECTURE.md §14)
build/
.gradle/
local.properties
*.iml
.idea/

# Maintainer's own device/app logs pulled while testing the app on real hardware (AGENTS.md §9 —
# these can contain device identifiers). Narrowed scope, ai-sessions/0043 (2026-09-22): an ad hoc
# individual debug-log/screenshot pull (not a full capture session) stays here, gitignored, never
# committed, and any of this project's own docs/commits must summarize findings from it directly
# rather than pointing back at a file here. A FULL hardware-capture session (recording + HCI snoop +
# app debug export/logcat + system log, i.e. everything CAPTURE_BLUETOOTH_HCI_SNOOP.md's own
# extraction step (§3) would call a capture) is moved to captures/CAP-NNN-*/ instead and committed
# there like any other capture — see that document's intro for the "third capture purpose" this
# covers (this project's own app under test, not the official app) and see DECISIONS.md ADR-037 for
# the decision retiring the old "always gitignored" rule for full sessions specifically.
android/logs/

# Reverse-engineering workspace: the pulled APK(s), decompiled output (JADX/apktool), and
# pbtk-extracted schemas are never committed to git — see AGENTS.md §4 ("Generated code is
# build-time only ... must never be committed to version control"), PROJECT.md's non-goals
# ("No distribution of the original Google APK or any part of it"), and PROJECT_RULES.md §8
# rule 20 (decompiled Java/smali is a reproduction of Google's copyrighted code, banned from
# this project's codebase even as research output — this holds even though it never leaves
# the maintainer's own machine, since "codebase" here means this git history). Git LFS does
# NOT exempt the APK file itself — anyone with repository access can still fetch an LFS
# object, which is still distribution. The whole tree below (one subfolder per analyzed APK
# version, per reverse-engineering/APK_VERSIONS.md) is ignored; only that small index file,
# tracked outside this tree, is committed.
reverse-engineering/apk/
*.apk

# APK-analysis tools under reverse-engineering/tools/<tool-name>/ (lambda_dispatcher_resolver,
# structural_index, and any future one built the same way): each tool's own Python source is
# tracked normally (original tooling code, not derived APK content), but its virtualenv/caches
# are not, and — same rule as above, same reason — none of them may ever gain a committed copy
# of decompiled smali/JADX output under its own tests/ directory either; every tool's test suite
# runs against the maintainer's local reverse-engineering/apk/<version>/ tree instead and skips
# itself when that tree isn't present (see each tool's own SPEC.md §11 and tests/).
reverse-engineering/tools/*/.venv/
reverse-engineering/tools/*/*.egg-info/
**/__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/

# OS/editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# to big
CAP-009-recording1.mp4
